  "summary": "Opinion columnist Jacob Sullum describes a bipartisan backlash against automated license plate readers, noting Texas Gov. Abbott froze state ALPR funding and Florida Gov. DeSantis called the technology 'out of control' after officer-misuse scandals. He cites Institute for Justice data that 181 local governments have canceled or declined to renew ALPR contracts since 2025, and discusses abuses, lax oversight, and calls for warrant requirements.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Institute for Justice counted 181 local governments that have canceled or declined to renew license plate reader contracts since the beginning of 2025",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "The police cannot police themselves",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "When I see, like, a police officer using this to track, like, an ex-girlfriend, I'm like, you know, what the hell's going on?",
